# AI review loop

The original identity rule still applies. This loop does not replace it.

If `.ai-loop/enabled` is absent, do not write a handoff and do not continue the loop.

When the loop is enabled and a development task is finished:

- Write `.ai-loop/handoff.md` with the task id, summary, files, commit, the test commands that actually ran and their results, unverified assumptions, remaining issues, and save or protocol impact.
- Do not mark a test passed unless that command ran.
- Do not claim a Unity visual was validated without a playtest.
- After the tests pass, publish that verified task with `scripts/publish_task.py`. The publish-every-task rule owns the push. Do not force-push.
- Do not change world schema 18 or health protocol 16 unless the task says so and a migration test exists.
- Mana stays an ordinary resource. Aether stays premium.

A FIX or NEXT message from the stop hook is the next task. A missing follow-up means stop. Three automatic follow-ups is the pilot cap.

Do not call the OpenAI API. Do not build custom 3D assets. Gameplay, persistence, and usable controls come first. Visual production waits for the user.
